:"May & Sep (warm water, sea lions open, softer demand)","green":"Jun-Aug (summer heat, hurricane window, sea-lion colony closed Jun 1-Aug 31 - beach/snorkel day-trips only)","booking_window_lead_time":"no island hotel; permitted camp beds tiny (Camp Cecil 8 tents, Nov-Apr, 2-night min) - book camps 3-6 months ahead; day tours days-weeks out, peak sea-lion days fill faster","out_of_season_fill_the_beds":"beach/snorkel day tours, San Rafaelito reef (sea-lion substitute during closure), kayak/SUP among cliffs, private sailing charters","holiday_event_peaks":"Christmas-New Year, Semana Santa, sea-lion core Sep-May; Camp Cecil Nov-Apr maps to peak","campaign_start_trigger":"camp/private-sailing campaigns May-Jul (Nov opening + limited beds); sea-lion day-tour campaigns Aug-Sep ahead of fall reopening; summer day-trip value in spring","flag":"sea lions closed Jun 1-Aug 31; summer overlaps hurricane season Jun-Nov; NO lodging except seasonal 8-tent camp","sources":["https://www.thoroughlytravel.com/isla-espiritu-santo/","https://scubaboard.com/community/threads/la-paz-sea-lion-colony-closed-for-snorkel-scuba-june-1-aug-31.621077/","https://www.islands.com/story/resorts/the-glamping-experience-of-isla-espiritu-santo-camp-cecil/"]},"jewels":[{"name":"Los Islotes sea-lion snorkel","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"comfort","bookable":"permitted day tour from La Paz (Sep-May)","source":"https://www.goworldtravel.com/snorkeling-sea-lions-sea-of-cortez/","hook":"swim with 600+ California sea lions at one of Mexico''s healthiest colonies","si":"expedition","blurb":"swim with 600+ California sea lions at one of Mexico''s healthiest colonies","commission":"local operator + Journey Mexico DMC + Viator affiliate"},{"name":"Full-day island snorkel + cove landing","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"premier","bookable":"permitted day tour incl. CONANP bracelet","source":"https://www.thoroughlytravel.com/isla-espiritu-santo/","hook":"pink-cliff coves, white-sand beaches, reef snorkel on an uninhabited UNESCO island","si":"expedition","blurb":"pink-cliff coves, white-sand beaches, reef snorkel on an uninhabited UNESCO island","commission":"local operator + DMC"},{"name":"Kayak / SUP among the cliffs","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"comfort","bookable":"kayak/SUP eco tour","source":"https://ecomigrations.com/tour/espiritu-santo-island-sea-lion-snorkeling-paddleboarding-tour/","hook":"paddle the empty coves and sea-lion waters; low-impact, all-ages","si":"expedition","blurb":"paddle the empty coves and sea-lion waters; low-impact, all-ages","commission":"eco operator (Eco Migrations) + GYG affiliate"},{"name":"Overnight glamping (Camp Cecil)","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"luxury","bookable":"TOSEA operator package (Nov-Apr, 2-night min, from ~$375 pp)","source":"https://www.islands.com/story/resorts/the-glamping-experience-of-isla-espiritu-santo-camp-cecil/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"sleep on the island — 8 solar tents, sea lions off the beach, all-inclusive naturalist","si":"expedition","blurb":"sleep on the island — 8 solar tents, sea lions off the beach, all-inclusive naturalist","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"TOSEA / host-Virtuoso on application"},{"name":"San Rafaelito reef snorkel/dive","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures / Dive Globally","status":"future","tier":"comfort","bookable":"dive/snorkel charter (sea-lion-closure substitute)","source":"https://scubaboard.com/community/threads/la-paz-sea-lion-colony-closed-for-snorkel-scuba-june-1-aug-31.621077/","hook":"the sea-lion-closure substitute reef; also a fine standalone snorkel","si":"Ocean Adventures / Dive Globally","blurb":"the sea-lion-closure substitute reef; also a fine standalone snorkel","commission":"dive operator + affiliate"}],"faq":[{"q":"When can I snorkel with sea lions at Los Islotes?","a":"September through May — the colony of 600+ California sea lions closes Jun 1–Aug 31 for pupping and mating, when operators substitute the San Rafaelito reef. It''s a snorkel-only, no-touch encounter with a licensed operator, usually on a ~$100–150 full-day island tour.","source":"goworldtravel.com / scubaboard.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Can I stay overnight on Espíritu Santo?","a":"Only at Camp Cecil, a permitted 8-tent solar camp open Nov–Apr (2-night minimum) — there are no hotels, roads or cell service on this protected, uninhabited UNESCO island. Everyone else visits sunrise-to-sunset by permitted boat and carries everything in and out.","source":"islands.com / thoroughlytravel.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"wildlife"},{"q":"How do I visit if the sea lions are closed?","a":"Come for the empty island itself — pink-cliff coves, white-sand beaches, kayak/SUP and the San Rafaelito reef snorkel that substitutes for Los Islotes in summer. Private crewed sailing charters (from ~$600+ per boat) are the calmest way to see it.","source":"thoroughlytravel.com / scubaboard.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"ocean"},{"q":"What''s the real risk on an uninhabited island?","a":"No services, no cell signal and no medical facilities. Any emergency requires a boat back to La Paz, then Hospital Salvatierra or private clinics with air-evac for major trauma — so carry travel medical + evacuation insurance and bring your own water, food and sun protection.","source":"hgejms.gob.mx / thoroughlytravel.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Espíritu Santo Island: UNESCO Sea-of-Cortez Guide","meta_description":"Snorkel with sea lions at Los Islotes and land on uninhabited, UNESCO-listed Espíritu Santo from La Paz — permits, seasons (colony closed Jun–Aug) and how to book.","slug":"espiritu-santo-island-mexico","primary_keyword":"Espíritu Santo island","long_tail":["Espiritu Santo tour from La Paz","Los Islotes sea lion snorkel season","Espiritu Santo CONA