ds 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro Federal Highway 15D State of Jalisco FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border with the state of Colima."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Year-round city destination; mild dry season Oct–May most comfortable","shoulder":"n/a (temperate, no beach swing)","green":"June–September summer rain (afternoon storms), still bookable","booking_lead":"Book ahead for FIL (Nov/Dec) and Mariachi festival (late Aug/early Sep) compression; leisure short-window","off_season_specials":"Rainy-season city-break + tequila-day-trip value; disclose afternoon storms","event_peaks":"Encuentro Internacional del Mariachi Aug 26–Sep 6 2026; FIL book fair Nov/Dec; Liga MX season (Chivas/Atlas)","campaign_start":"Mariachi packages by early summer; FIL culture packages by early fall; year-round tequila/city breaks"},"jewels":[{"name":"Tlaquepaque + El Parián","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Artisan pueblo of galleries + ceramics + covered plaza with evening mariachi","bookable_category":"guided craft/shopping tour + dining","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/guadalajara-jalisco-mexico/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"Year-round city destination","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"Artisan pueblo of galleries + ceramics + covered plaza with evening mariachi","when":"Year-round city destination","commission":"DMC / activity affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Tonalá Thu/Sun markets","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Street-wide artisan markets at near-production prices","bookable_category":"guided market tour + shipping","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/guadalajara-jalisco-mexico/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"Year-round city destination","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"Street-wide artisan markets at near-production prices","when":"Year-round city destination","commission":"DMC / activity affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Instituto Cultural Cabañas + Centro","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"UNESCO former hospice with Orozco murals, Teatro Degollado, cathedral","bookable_category":"walking tour","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/guadalajara-jalisco-mexico/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"Year-round city destination","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"UNESCO former hospice with Orozco murals, Teatro Degollado, cathedral","when":"Year-round city destination","commission":"activity affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"José Cuervo Express to Tequila","si_tag":"Culinary","status":"future","hook":"Saturday train to Tequila town — open bar + agave fields + distillery","bookable_category":"rail-tour ticket","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/guadalajara-jalisco-mexico/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"Year-round city destination","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culinary","blurb":"Saturday train to Tequila town — open bar + agave fields + distillery","when":"Year-round city destination","commission":"activity affiliate / DMC","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Birria + tortas ahogadas food crawl","si_tag":"Culinary","status":"future","hook":"The dish that started a global craze, at its source","bookable_category":"guided food tour","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.traveldojo.com/jalisco/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"Year-round city destination","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culinary","blurb":"The dish that started a global craze, at its source","when":"Year-round city destination","commission":"activity affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Mariachi Galas at Teatro Degollado","si_tag":"Live Entertainment","status":"future","hook":"World''s best mariachis + philharmonic, world''s largest festival Aug 26–Sep 6 2026","bookable_category":"gala tickets + hotel package","tier":"premier","source":"https://playersoflife.com/guadalajara/encuentro-internacional-del-mariachi-y-la-charreria-2026-agenda-completa-sedes-y-conciertos/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"Year-round city destination","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"entertainment","blurb":"World''s best mariachis + philharmonic, world''s largest festival Aug 26–Sep 6 2026","when":"Year-round city destination","commission":"ticketing/event affiliate + hotel","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Plaza de los Mariachis","si_tag":"Live Entertainment","status":"future","hook":"Hire live mariachi table-side in mariachi''s birthplace, free to browse","bookable_category":"free / pay per song, bundle with dining","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/guadalajara-jalisco-mexico/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"entertainment","blurb":"Hire live mariachi table-side in mariachi''s birthplace, free to browse","when":"year-round","commission":"bundle with dining/tour","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Chivas/Atlas at Estadio Akron","si_tag":"Sports","status":"future","hook":"Liga MX matchday, one of Mexico''s fiercest football rivalries","bookable_category":"match tickets + transfer","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/guadalajara-jalisco-mexico/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"Year-round city destination","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"sports","blurb":"Liga MX matchday, one of Mexico''s fiercest football rivalries","when":"Year-round city destination","commission":"ticketing/event affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-04"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for?","a":"Staying in the metro carve-out, not street crime. Fly into GDL (inside the carve-out), keep itineraries in the Guadalajara Metropolitan area, and don''t self-drive onto the restricted southern-Jalisco highways (Hwy 110, Hwy 80). The city itself calls for standard big-city precautions; altitude is gentle at ~1,590 m.","source":"travel.state.gov / planeta.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What is Guadalajara best known for culturally?","a":"Being the source of Mexico''s soul exports. It is the birthplace of modern mariachi (heard in original context at Plaza de los Mariachis), the artisan-ceramics capital via Tlaquepaque and Tonalá (markets Thu + Sun at near-production prices), and home to the UNESCO-listed Instituto Cultural Cabañas with Orozco murals.","source":"mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Can I do a tequila day trip from Guadalajara?","a":"Yes — the José Cuervo Express. The train runs Saturdays (some Sundays) from the metro to Tequila town with open bar, agave fields and a distillery stop; Guadalajara is also the source of birria and tortas ahogadas. Use organized operators — do not self-drive after tasting.","source":"mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"When is the mariachi festival, and is it worth planning around?","a":"Yes — it is the world''s largest, in mariachi''s birthplace. The Encuentro Internacional del Mariachi y la Charrería runs its 33rd edition Aug 26–Sep 6, 2026, with galas at Teatro Degollado; it and November''s FIL book fair are the two hotel-compression peaks, so book those windows early.","source":"playersoflife.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"entertainment"},{"q":"Is Colonia Americana worth a night out?","a":"Yes — it is repeatedly ranked among the world''s coolest neighborhoods. The Chapultepec/Lafayette district anchors the metro''s bar-and-restaurant density and its design-boutique hotels (Villa Ganz, Casa Habita, Hotel Demetria). Use rideshare or registered taxis at night, per standard big-city caution.","source":"mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"entertainment","si_fold_note":"folded from the retired `nightlife` slug into Global Live Entertainment 2026-08-23; the content is kept, the retired slug is not"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Guadalajara Travel Guide — Mariachi, Tequila & Tlaquepaque Crafts | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Mexico''s second city and the birthplace of mariachi: Plaza de los Mariachis, Tlaquepaque + Tonalá crafts, the José Cuervo tequila train, birria, and the FIL book fair. Bookable in the Guadalajara Metro carve-out.","slug":"guadalajara-mexico","primary_keyword":"Guadalajara travel guide","long_tail":["is Guadalajara safe to visit 2026","things to do in Guadalajara Mexico","Tlaquepaque and Tonalá crafts","José Cuervo Express tequila train","Encuentro Internacional del Mariachi dates","FIL Guadalajara book fair","boutique hotels Colonia Americana"],"search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Guadalajara","¿es seguro viajar a Guadalajara?","Tlaquepaque y Tonalá artesanías","José Cuervo Express boletos","Encuentro Internacional del Mariachi 2026 fechas","hoteles boutique Colonia Americana Guadalajara","Feria Internacional del Libro Guadalajara"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-04"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"culture","status":"future"},{"si":"culinary","status":"future"},{"si":"entertainment","status":"future"},{"si":"sports","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Casa Habita, a Member of Design Hotels","why_ultra":"Restored early-20th-c residence + new tower, library/restaurant, rooftop pool+bar, spa; Colonia Americana design-luxury boutique","earning":"on application / via host program","virtuoso_value_add":"verify (Design Hotels/Mr & Mrs Smith curation)","mor":true,"tier":"luxury boutique"},{"name":"Hotel Demetria","why_ultra":"Colonia Lafayette; gallery-like contemporary interiors, rooftop Sky Bar pool + terraces, city views","earning":"on application / via host program","virtuoso_value_add":"verify","mor":true,"tier":"luxury boutique"},{"name":"Villa Ganz Hotel Boutique","why_ultra":"Modern-colonial refuge, gardens + courtyards, top-rated small-luxury benchmark, Colonia Americana","earning":"on application / via host program","virtuoso_value_add":"verify","mor":true,"tier":"luxury boutique"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Guadalajara, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":20.6597,"lng":-103.3496}}'::jsonb, 58),
